UDP outbound + IPv4 pseudo-header L4 checksum helpers
=====================================================

`inet_send_udp` builds a full Ethernet/IPv4/UDP frame and hands
it to the nic. `inet_resolve_mac` picks the next-hop MAC; on
ARP miss the datagram is parked in the pending UDP queue so the
caller doesn't see a transient drop.

The pseudo-header checksum helpers are L4-shared (UDP requires,
TCP requires) but live here next to the sole non-TCP caller —
TCP's own use is module-internal in tcp.lsysl. PMTU-driven
fragmentation routes through `inet_pmtu_get`.

Same `oskit.servers` module as `inet_proto.lsysl`, so siblings
(frame pool, ARP cache, pending UDP queue, link-layer state)
resolve without imports.

    module oskit.servers

    import std.net.{ETHERTYPE_IPV4, IP_PROTO_UDP,
        pkt_read_u16, pkt_write_u16, pkt_write_mac, pkt_write_ipv4,
        net_checksum, ipv4, ipv4_octet}


### L4 checksum helpers (IPv4 pseudo-header)

Core one's-complement sum over `pseudo-header + L4 header +
payload`. Pseudo-header layout (12 bytes): src_ip (4) + dst_ip
(4) + zero (1) + proto (1) + l4_len (2). The L4 bytes come
straight from the frame buffer at `[l4_off .. l4_off + l4_len)`
— caller decides whether the checksum field there is zero (for
transmit) or stored (for receive-side verify).

Returns the folded 16-bit sum (not complemented). Valid transmit
frames have the complement stored in their checksum field;
receive-side verification expects this helper to return `0xffff`
when the stored checksum is correct. Shared by UDP (proto=17)
and TCP (proto=6).

    inet_l4_partial_sum(src_ip: u32, dst_ip: u32, proto: int,
                        frame: *byte, l4_off: int, l4_len: int) -> int
        var sum = 0
        sum += (ipv4_octet(src_ip, 0) << 8) | ipv4_octet(src_ip, 1)
        sum += (ipv4_octet(src_ip, 2) << 8) | ipv4_octet(src_ip, 3)
        sum += (ipv4_octet(dst_ip, 0) << 8) | ipv4_octet(dst_ip, 1)
        sum += (ipv4_octet(dst_ip, 2) << 8) | ipv4_octet(dst_ip, 3)
        sum += proto
        sum += l4_len
        var i = 0
        while i + 1 < l4_len
            sum += pkt_read_u16(frame, l4_off + i)
            i += 2
        if i < l4_len
            sum += (int(frame[l4_off + i]) & 0xff) << 8
        while (sum >> 16) != 0
            sum = (sum & 0xffff) + (sum >> 16)
        sum


Transmit-side helper. Caller must zero the UDP checksum field in
`frame` before calling. A computed 0 maps to `0xffff` so the
written value never collides with the "no checksum" sentinel
(RFC 768).

    inet_udp_checksum(src_ip: u32, dst_ip: u32,
                     frame: *byte, udp_off: int, udp_len: int) -> int
        val s = inet_l4_partial_sum(src_ip, dst_ip, IP_PROTO_UDP,
                                    frame, udp_off, udp_len)
        val c = (~s) & 0xffff
        if c == 0
            return 0xffff
        c


Receive-side verify. Frame still carries its sender-written
checksum; a valid packet folds to `0xffff`. A stored 0 means
"no checksum" (accept unconditionally, IPv4-only). Returns 1
on valid, 0 on corrupt.

    inet_udp_verify(src_ip: u32, dst_ip: u32,
                   frame: *byte, udp_off: int, udp_len: int) -> int
        val stored = pkt_read_u16(frame, udp_off + 6)
        if stored == 0
            return 1
        val s = inet_l4_partial_sum(src_ip, dst_ip, IP_PROTO_UDP,
                                    frame, udp_off, udp_len)
        if s == 0xffff
            return 1
        0


### UDP — outbound

Builds a full Ethernet/IPv4/UDP frame and hands it to the nic.
`inet_resolve_mac` picks the next-hop MAC: the destination's own
cached MAC for on-subnet targets, the gateway's for off-subnet.
Cache miss fires an ARP request; we park the datagram in the
pending UDP queue so `inet_arp_drain_pending` can retry it when
the reply arrives, and report success to the caller. Returns -1
only for hard failures (link not ready, `dlen` out of range, nic
rejection, or pending queue full).

UDP checksum is computed over the IPv4 pseudo-header + UDP header
+ payload — required for IPv6 peers and recommended for IPv4.

    inet_send_udp(owner_tid: int, dst_ip: u32, dst_port: int, src_port: int, data: *byte, dlen: int) -> int
        if inet_our_mac_known == 0
            return -1
        if dlen < 0
            return -1
        if dlen > 1472
            return -1

Limited broadcast (255.255.255.255) skips ARP — there is no
"MAC of the broadcast address", we simply transmit with
Ethernet dst = `ff:ff:ff:ff:ff:ff`. We also force IP src =
`0.0.0.0` and the UDP pseudo-header src to 0: DHCP clients
(RFC 2131 §4.1) must use 0.0.0.0 until they bind a lease,
because the addr they want to use is what they are asking for.

        val bcast_all = ipv4(255, 255, 255, 255)
        val is_bcast = dst_ip == bcast_all
        var next_hop_mac: [6]byte
        if is_bcast
            var bi = 0
            while bi < 6
                next_hop_mac[bi] = byte(0xff)
                bi += 1
        else
            if inet_resolve_mac(dst_ip, next_hop_mac) == 0
                // ARP miss: park the datagram; the reply handler
                // will retransmit it. Returning -1 only if the
                // pending queue is full.
                if inet_queue_pending_udp(owner_tid, dst_ip, dst_port, src_port, data, dlen) != 0
                    return dlen
                return -1

Effective MTU. PMTU cache lookup; default = link MTU when no
entry exists for this destination. The cache is keyed by dst_ip,
so a test can seed an entry against 255.255.255.255 to drive the
fragmentation path without depending on ARP resolution; in the
typical case nothing is cached and the lookup returns link MTU,
which keeps the single-fragment fast path active.

        val eff_mtu = inet_pmtu_get(dst_ip)

        var pseudo_src = inet_get_our_ip()
        if is_bcast
            pseudo_src = u32(0)

        val ip_ident = inet_next_ip_id()
        val ip_total = 20 + 8 + dlen      // single-fragment IP total length

Single-fragment fast path: the entire `ETH+IP+UDP+payload` fits
within `eff_mtu` after adding the IP header. No frag flags, no
offset, MF=0. This is the path traffic takes any time the cache
either has no entry for the destination or learned an MTU large
enough to swallow the full datagram.

        if ip_total <= eff_mtu
            val fidx = inet_frame_alloc()
            val frame = inet_frame_buf(fidx)
            val total_len = 14 + ip_total

            pkt_write_mac(frame, 0, next_hop_mac)
            pkt_write_mac(frame, 6, inet_our_mac)
            pkt_write_u16(frame, 12, ETHERTYPE_IPV4)

            frame[14] = 0x45
            frame[15] = 0
            pkt_write_u16(frame, 16, ip_total)
            pkt_write_u16(frame, 18, ip_ident)
            pkt_write_u16(frame, 20, 0)
            frame[22] = 64
            frame[23] = byte(IP_PROTO_UDP)
            pkt_write_u16(frame, 24, 0)
            if is_bcast
                pkt_write_ipv4(frame, 26, 0, 0, 0, 0)
            else
                pkt_write_ipv4(frame, 26,
                    INET_OUR_IP_A, INET_OUR_IP_B, INET_OUR_IP_C, INET_OUR_IP_D)
            pkt_write_ipv4(frame, 30, ipv4_octet(dst_ip, 0), ipv4_octet(dst_ip, 1), ipv4_octet(dst_ip, 2), ipv4_octet(dst_ip, 3))
            pkt_write_u16(frame, 24, net_checksum(frame + 14, 20))

            pkt_write_u16(frame, 34, src_port)
            pkt_write_u16(frame, 36, dst_port)
            pkt_write_u16(frame, 38, 8 + dlen)
            pkt_write_u16(frame, 40, 0)
            var i = 0
            while i < dlen
                frame[42 + i] = data[i]
                i += 1
            pkt_write_u16(frame, 40,
                inet_udp_checksum(pseudo_src, dst_ip, frame, 34, 8 + dlen))

            val rc = inet_nic_send_packet(frame, total_len)
            inet_frame_release(fidx)
            return rc

Fragmentation path (RFC 791 §3.2). The full L4 datagram is
`UDP_header(8) + payload(dlen)` bytes; we stage it in
`inet_udp_egress_buf`, compute the UDP checksum over the whole
datagram, then walk the buffer in slices of `frag_payload`
bytes, emitting one IP fragment per slice. Non-final slice
sizes must be 8-byte multiples so `frag_offset` (in 8-byte
units) lands on a boundary. The last fragment carries whatever
remains and clears the MF flag.

        var staging: [1480]byte
        pkt_write_u16(staging, 0, src_port)
        pkt_write_u16(staging, 2, dst_port)
        pkt_write_u16(staging, 4, 8 + dlen)
        pkt_write_u16(staging, 6, 0)
        var bi = 0
        while bi < dlen
            staging[8 + bi] = data[bi]
            bi += 1
        pkt_write_u16(staging, 6,
            inet_udp_checksum(pseudo_src, dst_ip, staging, 0, 8 + dlen))

        val total_l4 = 8 + dlen
        var frag_payload = ((eff_mtu - 20) / 8) * 8
        if frag_payload < 8
            frag_payload = 8

        var off = 0
        while off < total_l4
            var this_len = total_l4 - off
            var more = 0
            if this_len > frag_payload
                this_len = frag_payload
                more = 1

            val fidx = inet_frame_alloc()
            val frame = inet_frame_buf(fidx)

            pkt_write_mac(frame, 0, next_hop_mac)
            pkt_write_mac(frame, 6, inet_our_mac)
            pkt_write_u16(frame, 12, ETHERTYPE_IPV4)

            frame[14] = 0x45
            frame[15] = 0
            pkt_write_u16(frame, 16, 20 + this_len)
            pkt_write_u16(frame, 18, ip_ident)
            val flags_frag = (more << 13) | (off / 8)
            pkt_write_u16(frame, 20, flags_frag)
            frame[22] = 64
            frame[23] = byte(IP_PROTO_UDP)
            pkt_write_u16(frame, 24, 0)
            if is_bcast
                pkt_write_ipv4(frame, 26, 0, 0, 0, 0)
            else
                pkt_write_ipv4(frame, 26,
                    INET_OUR_IP_A, INET_OUR_IP_B, INET_OUR_IP_C, INET_OUR_IP_D)
            pkt_write_ipv4(frame, 30, ipv4_octet(dst_ip, 0), ipv4_octet(dst_ip, 1), ipv4_octet(dst_ip, 2), ipv4_octet(dst_ip, 3))
            pkt_write_u16(frame, 24, net_checksum(frame + 14, 20))

            var k = 0
            while k < this_len
                frame[34 + k] = staging[off + k]
                k += 1

            inet_nic_send_packet(frame, 14 + 20 + this_len)
            inet_frame_release(fidx)
            inet_frag_egress_count += 1

            off += this_len
        dlen


